PROBLEM
-------
Every PRODUCTION API call returns errorCode 270202 "no permission for
this brand", on every endpoint, for brandId 200.

Authentication itself succeeds. See the control cases below:
  * omitting brandId returns a DIFFERENT error (270201 "brandId is
    required"), so the server reads and validates our request;
  * signing with a wrong secret returns HTTP 401 AUTHORIZATION SIGNATURE
    ERROR, so our signature IS being accepted in every other case;
  * the SAME client code, against ACC with the ACC credentials, works and
    returns devices. So our signature algorithm is correct.

This points to brand 200 having no binding to this accessKey on your side.

REQUEST
-------
Please bind brand "Kayve" (brandId 200) to accessKey
1095d44693c7c147d698c3aab70de90287 on lockservice.whaletv.com.

The brandId above is not a guess: it comes from your own portal. Logged in
at https://lockservice.whaletv.com as tech@kayvegroup.com, the web UI calls
  GET /lock-portal/lock/device/brandList
which responds:
  {"data":[{"brandId":"200","brandName":"Kayve","productList":[],
   "subDataDefault":null}],"errorCode":"0","errorMsg":null}

Note that the web portal does NOT send brandId in its own requests (e.g.
GET /lock-portal/lock/device/page?pageNum=1&pageSize=10): it resolves the
brand from the logged-in user. That is why the portal works for us while
the Open API does not.

The devices we need to manage are visible in that portal right now, e.g.
54:01:4A:16:35:78, 54:01:4A:16:35:79, B4:04:29:7E:3A:ED, 84:93:EC:87:12:71.

